{
  "captured_at": "2026-07-25T18:15:12",
  "providers": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Groq",
      "api_base": "",
      "description": "**Pros**: Blazing fast LPU (Language Processing Unit) inference; ideal for real-time, low-latency applications using open-weight models.\n\n**Cons**: Strict free-tier bottlenecks, typically capped at 30 requests per minute (RPM).\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Groq strictly enforces both RPM and Tokens Per Minute (TPM); hitting either threshold triggers a 429 error. By rotating multiple Groq keys in a round-robin setup, we can pool your TPM allowances and easily bypass the 30 RPM ceiling, maintaining continuous ultra-fast inference.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "name": "Google",
      "api_base": "",
      "description": "**Pros**: Unlocks massive context windows (up to 2 million tokens) and highly generous free-tier usage limits.\n\n**Cons**: Data processed on the free tier may be used to train Google's models. Note: As highlighted in your setup, only Gemma models are currently working.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Free accounts are typically restricted to 15 RPM and 1 million TPM, alongside daily caps. Load-balancing across multiple Google API keys prevents any individual account from hitting the 15 RPM limit, ensuring long-context queries flow smoothly without timeouts.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "name": "Cerebras",
      "api_base": "",
      "description": "**Pros**: Unmatched Wafer-Scale Engine (WSE) speed (up to 1,800+ tokens/second). Exceptionally efficient for heavy batch processing.\n\n**Cons**: The free tier restricts RPM heavily (often 5\u201330 RPM). Note: Accessing certain models (like Gemma-4-31B) requires a verified payment card on file for the trial.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Cerebras uses a dual-bucket system tracking both RPM and TPM (uncached vs. total tokens). Multiplexing several Cerebras keys allows to pool uncached TPM allowances and bypass the tight RPM bottlenecks on massive models.\n\n**Note**: Gemma-4-31B needs payment card to work.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "name": "OpenRouter",
      "api_base": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
      "description": "**Pros**: A powerful aggregator offering access to over 20 free models (using the :free suffix) via a single standardized API. No data training occurs on free endpoints.\n\n**Cons**: Free endpoints have rigid daily request ceilings (often 50\u2013200/day) and rely entirely on the stability of the upstream provider.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy:** OpenRouter limits free accounts strictly at 20 RPM, alongside low daily caps. Spreading requests across multiple OpenRouter keys via LiteLLM allows to stack these daily quotas, circumventing the restrictive account-level ceilings.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "name": "Mistral",
      "api_base": "",
      "description": "**Pros**: High-quality open-weight models (like Codestral and Mistral Large) optimized for coding and complex logic workloads.\n\n**Cons**: Data submitted on the \"Experiment\" free tier may be used for model training. Rate limits also dynamically fluctuate based on Mistral's network load.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Mistral enforces varying RPM and TPM limits depending on current server capacity. Since free-tier keys are heavily throttled during peak hours, cycling through multiple keys ensures automatic failover, allowing LiteLLM to seamlessly retry stalled requests on an unthrottled key.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "name": "Cohere",
      "api_base": "",
      "description": "**Pros**: Industry-leading enterprise models explicitly specialized for Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Command R/R+), alongside top-tier Embed and Rerank endpoints.\n\n**Cons**: The Free Trial tier is restricted to non-commercial use only and is heavily throttled.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Cohere imposes very tight concurrency and RPM limits (often 10\u201320 RPM). By configuring multiple Cohere API keys in load balancer, instantly expand the pipeline's capacity, preventing constant 429 timeout errors during intensive RAG document processing workflows.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "name": "Ollama",
      "api_base": "https://api.ollama.com",
      "description": "**Pros**: Privacy-first architecture. The newly expanded Ollama Cloud tier offloads massive models to cloud GPUs for free, requiring no local hardware while maintaining local tool compatibility.\n\n**Cons**: The Free plan strictly limits cloud model execution to just one concurrent session at a time.\n\n**Rate Limit Strategy**: Instead of standard RPM, Ollama Cloud enforces strict concurrency limits (1 concurrent model slot per free account). Distributing requests across multiple Ollama Cloud API keys enables parallel processing, effectively bypassing the single-slot queue limitation for multi-agent workflows.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-23 11:24:46"
    }
  ],
